US915 first-uplink panic after a DR4 join and a 125-kHz-only CFList
================================================================

Captured naturally on 2026-10-15 at 22:28:29 EDT (2026-10-16 02:28:29 UTC).
Third fresh BLE reset in this capture batch; the network was a third-party
network with no test-side gateway or server configuration changes.

Unfixed SWL2001 revision: 33870e4ff46b0117a47e60d2ebba8e8e25ba2ce2
ESP32 HAL wrapper revision: 0714774590e0a522e48399b9f33ade1642c3f470
Firmware ELF SHA256: 987cde3a8aaec13adb3d4315ca6a29c1cfc5db5897e8ab9d5e0d3beaf4c58550
Saved-bank preference and join control were disabled. Existing modem tracing
and failure diagnostics were enabled. A HAL logging change routed task-context
radio traces through the ESP logging hook into the existing Wi-Fi RAM log.

This extract contains the radio sequence, complete no-channel diagnostic, and
stored panic event. Device keys, unrelated application logs, and addresses of
local services have been omitted. Fragment order is preserved.

Observed failure
----------------
The eighteenth completed JoinRequest used DR4/SF8/BW500 at 904600000 Hz.
JOINED was reported at 277753 ms; the panic followed at 277873 ms (120 ms later).
JoinAccept applied CFList 00 FF 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 01,
enabling only 125-kHz channels 8-15 and disabling every 500-kHz channel.
The retained ADR rate and selected first-uplink rate were still DR4, although
the applied mask supported only DR0-DR3. The selector exhausted 224 trials
and fell back to DR4. No channel was both enabled and DR4-compatible.
No LinkADR command had been applied.

Two DR0 requests on the eventually enabled bank (904700000 and 903900000 Hz)
completed and were followed by JOINFAIL. These device logs do not establish
why the network did not complete those joins.

Host regression before the fix
------------------------------
The [LoRaWANCapturedPanic] host test drives the actual JoinAccept completion
and first-uplink channel selection using the captured join DR/frequency and
CFList. The unfixed run reproduced retained DR4, selected DR4, zero eligible
channels, region_us_915_get_next_channel panic, and the 224-trial fallback.

